    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d279-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0454" n="412" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg412"/>

                <head>Mr. Dudley to Mr.
                        Edwards.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Liverpool</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 3, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to my application made to you so
                    long since as the seventh day of July last, to detain a steam iron-clad ram
                    built by Messrs. Laird for the confederates, and launched on the fourth of July
                    last, I have now to inform you that intelligence on which I place full reliance
                    has reached me that the vessel is taking coal on board, and I apprehend that she
                    may go to sea at any time unless detained.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS H. DUDLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Price Edwards</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Collector</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
